  "notes": "Schools follow the French national programmes and class names, overseen by the Service de l'éducation nationale de Saint-Barthélemy et de Saint-Martin (SENIDN) of the Académie de la Guadeloupe. The island has primary schools (one public, two private under contract) and one collège, Mireille Choisy, which also runs a 2de générale et technologique class; there is no lycée, so 1re and Terminale are taken off the island. Maternelle is left out, so CP (age 6) is year 1. The brevet closes 3e and the baccalauréat closes Terminale."
